**API contract change — `POST /search`**

Before:
```jsonc
// Request
{
  "query": "book" // Required string.
}

// Response
{
  "result": {
    "items": [
      {"id": "a"}
    ]
  }
}
```

After, existing behavior:
```jsonc
// Request
{
  "query": "book"
  // include_tags is optional; omission defaults to false.
  // Explicit "include_tags": false produces the same response.
}

// Response — unchanged for omission or false.
{
  "result": {
    "items": [
      {"id": "a"}
      // tags remains omitted, not null.
    ]
  }
}
```

After, opted-in behavior:
```jsonc
// Request
{
  "query": "book",
  "include_tags": true // New optional boolean; requests tags.
}

// Response
{
  "result": {
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "tags": ["sale"] // Added only when opted in; always a string list.
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

An opted-in item with no tags returns `"tags": []`; an empty result retains `"items": []`. The `result.items` envelope is preserved. Unknown request keys remain ignored.

